# BotMarket prod crontab (R1, docs/cost-plan.md). Install on the VPS with:
#   crontab deploy/crontab
# (or merge these three lines into an existing crontab — check `crontab -l`
# first so you don't clobber anything else already scheduled there).
#
# Edit REPO_DIR below if this repo doesn't live at /opt/botmarket. Both
# scripts source REPO_DIR/.env.prod themselves for secrets (CRON_SECRET,
# DOMAIN, RCLONE_REMOTE, ...) — nothing sensitive is typed into this file.

REPO_DIR=/opt/botmarket

# Crash-loop alert sweep (specs/02-architecture.md) — same schedule as
# apps/web/vercel.json's Vercel Cron entry.
*/5 * * * * $REPO_DIR/deploy/cron-hit.sh /api/cron/degraded-alerts >> /var/log/botmarket-cron.log 2>&1

# Supervisor heartbeat sweep (docs/decisions.md, 2026-07-23) — catches "the
# whole runtime container/process is down or never started," which the
# crash-loop alert above can't: that one only fires from inside the
# supervisor's own reconcile loop, so a supervisor that dies before that
# loop even starts (bad env var, startup exception) never produces anything
# for it to alert on. Every minute, not every 5 — this failure mode takes
# every customer's bot down at once. Same schedule as apps/web/vercel.json's
# Vercel Cron entry (Hobby-plan Vercel deploys can't run cron this often —
# per-minute schedules need a paid plan; the VPS crontab path has no such
# limit).
* * * * * $REPO_DIR/deploy/cron-hit.sh /api/cron/supervisor-health >> /var/log/botmarket-cron.log 2>&1

# Retention sweep (R3, docs/cost-plan.md) — same schedule as vercel.json.
47 4 * * * $REPO_DIR/deploy/cron-hit.sh /api/cron/retention >> /var/log/botmarket-cron.log 2>&1

# Nightly Postgres backup (R1) — before the retention sweep, so a backup
# always reflects pre-retention data.
17 3 * * * cd $REPO_DIR && ./deploy/backup.sh >> /var/log/botmarket-backup.log 2>&1
